-.\" TODO: document TCL_EVAL_INVOKE and TCL_EVAL_NOERR.
+.TP 23
+\fBTCL_EVAL_INVOKE\fR
+.
+This flag is only used by \fBTcl_EvalObjv\fR and \fBTcl_NREvalObjv\fR; it
+is ignored by other procedures.  It is intended for commands such as aliases
+and ensembles that dispatch to another command on behalf of their caller.
+The first word of \fIobjv\fR is resolved in the global namespace instead of
+the current namespace (the variable context is not changed), no
+.QW "while executing"
+line is added to the \fB\-errorinfo\fR return option if the command fails,
+and the information used to rewrite ensemble error messages is preserved.
+.TP 23
+\fBTCL_EVAL_NOERR\fR
+.
+This flag is only used by \fBTcl_EvalObjv\fR and \fBTcl_NREvalObjv\fR; it
+is ignored by other procedures.  If this flag bit is set, no exception
+processing is done at all: no information is added to the
+\fB\-errorinfo\fR return option, and when called at the top level, a
+\fBTCL_RETURN\fR, \fBTCL_BREAK\fR or \fBTCL_CONTINUE\fR result is returned
+to the caller unchanged instead of being converted.  The caller is
+expected to do any such processing itself.
 
